A||||12||William||New kenwood 4x10's?||||1||
Z||000000||William||11-28-2000||09:55 AM||||Anyone try the kenwoods with the new style tweeter? After installing the new head unit, I was able to blow out my old dry rotted kenwoods and now need replacements. Locally, my choices are the 2 way 4x10 pioneers or the new style 4x10 kenwoods. The old kenwoods had a paper tweeter and I was not happy with dull sounding treble response. Has anyone actually heard and compared these 2 speakers? I'm suspicious of the paper cone tweeter in the pioneer. Does it put out much treble? The new kenwoods now have a polymide dome tweeter and I'm guessing that would do A better job. Has anyone heard them yet or have comments on that style tweeter? AS far as componets, I will not be using a sub, and therefore need all the bass I can get. I was satisfied with the bass I got from old kenwoods,(No rap here!)<BR>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||stimpy||11-28-2000||10:03 AM||||Well, if you could be happy with the bass from any 4x10, my money would be on the Pioneer. Haven't heard the Kenwood, have the Pioneer because every time I have compared brands of replacement speakers Pioneer put out the sound I like. And I do like BASS.<P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||William||11-28-2000||10:19 AM||||Mabye saying satisfied is a little to strong but the bass is close enough that I'd rather not deal with the subs. Below is a pic of the new kenwoods for those that have not seen them yet.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.kenwoodusa.com/img/products_l/KFC-415C.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||2xsess||11-28-2000||10:26 AM||||Wiliam, I have a set of them. Unfortunetly they were the display set and one of them seems to be a bit blown. I haven't had the time to take them back yet. The treble is good. I've had the pioneers before and to my untrained ear they both sound great. I would say that the bass is better on the pioneers but, I'd need to get my blown speaker replaced before I could give you a true idea. <P>Jeff||||reg||1
Z||000004||William||11-28-2000||10:36 AM||||So you feel the treble is simular between these 2 models? I would be interested in hearing your final opinion when the speaker gets replaced.<BR>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000005||overlord||11-28-2000||12:45 PM||||i have those in my fiero...had them for about a year now and they sound great...<P>I was impressed on how they sounded compapred to the factory ones.||||reg||1
Z||000006||overlord||11-28-2000||12:47 PM||||in my opinion...kenwood speakers always sounded more "crisp" compared to pioneers.<P>when i bought the kenwoods, i had a chance to listen to both pioneer and kenwood...and the pioneers werent as crisp and sharp for treble.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Seanh||11-28-2000||01:08 PM||||Pioneer's and Kenwoods are both really good speakers. I would'nt touch a paper cone speaker (or tweeter) with a 10 foot pole, on any brand. Although your high's may be comprimised a little with a paper cone, the main factor is durability. They wont last near as long as some other compounds they use. I am not sure on Kenwoods off hand, but Pioneer uses Liquid Crystal Fiber (Polyarylate), and IMPP cones. If you are looking for some good bass in the Fiero, I would say go with 6x9's. They will put out more bass then any 4x10 will. I would reccomend the Pioneer 4-ways. They sound awesome. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Master_Sushi||11-29-2000||12:14 AM||||I guess I should have waited a few weeks before buying my pioneers. O well...<P>I got the pioneer 4X10's a week ago and they sound great to me. They have a paper tweeter but lower freq response then the kenwood 4X10's I was looking at.<p>[This message has been edited by Master_Sushi (edited 11-29-2000).]||||reg||4
Z||000009||2M4 Dale||11-29-2000||12:23 AM||||I have those "new" 4"x10" Kenwoods in my Fiero along with Kenwood Excellons 4"x6" in the sail panels...I have a Jenson head unit and CD changer with a Pheonix Gold Saphire amp and a Power Accoustic 8" sub..........I think my system sounds great !!!||||reg||1
Z||000010||William||11-29-2000||12:35 AM||||Hey Overlord,<BR>When you made this comparison, were you listening to the 4x10's of each brand? Also, how do you feel the bass compared. So far it seems that the pioneers wins in bass and the kenwoods get the treble award? I asume we're talking about the new style kenwoods right?||||reg||1
Z||000011||sqoach||11-29-2000||12:37 AM||||i got some rockford 4x10s from radio shack that were on display and they've sounded great since i bought them.  they don't have that cheap paper tweater either, which is probably why the highs sound good.  i only paid $50 for both of 'em  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh||||reg||6
Z||000012||overlord||11-29-2000||08:55 AM||||ya william..<BR>i listened to both the 4*10's.<BR>i wouldnt say the pioneers had more bass.....but just less treble..<P>I'm  quite impressed on how these little speakers sound bass wise actually.<BR>Put it this way, when i first got them in with new head unit...my cousin is like "wow..you dont need any subwoofers.."<P>and then once i did get a sub..."his wow turned  into a HOLY SH*T".  That was when both of us had never really heard a subwoofer.<P>anyways.....i bought the KENWOODS  cause i liked the crisper sound.||||reg||1
